60,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option A seems the kindest to the treasurer. They only have to collect the money once.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A is the most stable for the budget, but we know from the bank statements that lump sums are a problem.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option A and C are too rigid. They create a clear boundary that might discourage newcomers from drifting in.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,Option B is a nightmare. Imagine having to pay every time you want to see your friends! No wonder people are hesitant.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B is the only one that actually addresses the unfairness. If you don't come, you don't pay. Simple.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, but wouldn't Option B make the treasurer's job much harder? I saw the logs; it's a lot of work.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,@Minato is right. Option B is a logistical disaster. Option C provides a middle ground for stability and flexibility.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Option C still categorizes people. Once you are in a ""tier,"" you are labeled. That changes the social dynamic.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, Option C is just a fancy way of saying ""some of us are more important than others."" It's not very charming.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the treasurer's stress is a small price to pay for ending the resentment of the people actually running the place.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I really feel bad for the treasurer. I think I'll vote for Option A to keep things simple and peaceful.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot support Option B. It's too volatile. Option C allows us to secure the fixed costs while offering options.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I will vote for Option B. Despite the work, it is the only way to let people join and leave without a heavy commitment.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I can't stand the idea of a ""pay-per-visit"" vibe. I'll go with Option A. Let's just pay it and forget about it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, that's exactly the problem. You ""forget about it"" because you aren't the one cleaning up after everyone else.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
